            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Deb C"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This pilaf makes a wonderful side dish. Its flavor will not overshadow the main dish, but can easily be adjusted if you would like a pilaf with more jazz. This is a good, basic pilaf. I used my homemade chicken broth which is more flavorful than the store bought kind, and used butter instead of vegetable oil for sautéing the onion. I chose this recipe to use up some nearly empty packages of rice, so this was a combination of basmati rice and long grain white rice, and it worked out very well. Thanks Carol for sharing!",
            "datePublished": "2014-08-01T13:32:15.343Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "cooking41"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Absolutely delicious, and the secret to it is using basmati rice. It cooks up perfectly, and doesn't leave you feeling bloated, as happens with other types of rice I have used. I added some minced garlic to the onions and bay leaf, and a touch of black pepper. I used chicken stock this time, and plan to use the beef stock in the future if it goes with a beef dish. Many thanks, Carol, for sharing this with us.",
            "datePublished": "2015-11-20T14:10:32.750Z"
          },
